---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a release that removes a file of the blueprint reaches the project's own lines
    accDescr: A pull request of the blueprint removes a file of the blueprint. The job update of the Variants workflow fails it until MOVED of blueprint/migrate.py names the file and the one that takes its place. After the release, the update deletes the file, and the step Files of the project finds each line of the project that still names it. A page of Markdown is changed by migrate --fix, which the fix bot commits onto the update. Any other line is a warning and a step of the checklist for you, and a line with blueprint: keep in a comment stays as it is. Then the update merges itself.

    removed(["A pull request of the<br>blueprint removes a file"])
    guard{"Variants, update:<br>does MOVED name it?"}
    entry["Add it to MOVED, with<br>the file that takes its place"]
    update["After the release, the<br>update deletes the file"]
    step{"Step Files of the project:<br>which line names it?"}
    page["A page of Markdown:<br>migrate --fix changes only<br>the path, the fix bot<br>commits it"]
    other["Any other line: a warning<br>and a step of the checklist"]
    kept["A line with<br>blueprint: keep stays"]
    merged(["The update<br>merges itself"])

    removed --> guard
    guard -- "no: the check fails" --> entry --> guard
    guard -- "yes" --> update --> step
    step --> page --> merged
    step --> other --> merged
    step --> kept --> merged

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class removed,guard,update,step,page bot
    class entry,other,kept you
    class merged done
